1. Improve Time Management & Task Prioritization

Desired Improvement:
Consistently deliver tasks on time without over-polishing or missing deadlines.

Plan to Achieve:

Break all assigned work into milestones with internal due dates.

Use daily task prioritization based on impact and urgency.

Provide early check-ins for work that may risk delays.

Metrics for Success:

95–100% of tasks delivered on or before their due dates.

Fewer last-minute deadline extensions.

Positive feedback from leadership on delivery consistency.

2. Strengthen Communication & Ownership

Desired Improvement:
Improve proactive communication and ownership of tasks from start to completion.

Plan to Achieve:

Provide regular status updates during standups and via Teams/Slack.

Raise risks or blockers immediately when identified.

Take full ownership of assigned tasks, including follow-ups and documentation.

Metrics for Success:

Consistent weekly status reporting without reminders.

Reduced rework due to miscommunication.

Improved feedback from team and manager on clarity and accountability.

3. Enhance Security Alignment & Code Release Readiness

Desired Improvement:
Improve effectiveness in security alignment, SonarQube handling, and release preparedness.

Plan to Achieve:

Conduct weekly research on security best practices around certificates, encryption, and vulnerabilities.

Ensure SonarQube findings are reviewed promptly and true positives are ticketed on time.

Review release documentation and participate in rollback walkthroughs to improve independent release readiness.

Metrics for Success:

Timely creation of Sonar/SAST tickets within SLA.

Increased confidence handling release processes independently.

Fewer security-related delays during releases.
